              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for present, then the Mandarin for to give as a present."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 一会儿",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "一会儿 — yíhuìr — \"a little while; in a moment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "我一会儿打电话 wǒ yíhuìr dǎ diànhuà — I'll ring in a little while."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 会 (huì) — 人 spread as a roof, two bars, and a bend with a dot. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "yī changes its tone here, rising to yí before the falling huì: yíhuìr."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "一会儿 (yíhuìr) is built from 一 'one', huì and the ending r, inherited from Middle Chinese, 'jit, hwajH and nye (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). The dictionary glosses huì as 'to come together'; how the phrase came to mean a short while is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for times and partings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
